      "instruction": "Why does a passing siren change pitch?",
      "explanation": "Subsonic straight moving source in still uniform medium, stationary roadside listener. Received frequency computed at retarded emission time, not source position at reception. Collinear coincidence undefined. Representative sparse wavefronts are illustrative, not one circle per audio cycle. No actual audio or shock waves."
